@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
!include style.iuml
title Downloaded File - observation, management, and resolution
top to bottom direction
state "Identified candidate" as Identified
state "Ready candidate" as Ready
state "Managed file" as Managed {
  state Organized
  state InReview
  state Kept
  state Snoozed
  Organized -down-> InReview : Review completes\n[age due]
  Snoozed --> InReview : Review completes\n[snooze elapsed]
  InReview -down-> Kept : Keep completes
  InReview -right-> Snoozed : Snooze completes\n/ defer seven days
  Organized --> Kept : undo Organize [E]\n/ original location
  InReview --> Snoozed : undo Review [E]\n/ prior location; +7 days
  Kept --> InReview : undo Keep [E]
  Snoozed --> InReview : undo Snooze [E]
}
state Moved
state Recycled
state Missing
[*] --> Identified : discover a top-level candidate
Identified --> Identified : excluded or not ready\n/ leave untouched
Identified --> Ready : eligible readiness observation
Ready --> Identified : recheck no longer ready\nor preview content changed
Ready --> Organized : Organize completes\n[consent covers folder]
InReview --> Moved : confirmed Move\ncompletes
InReview --> Recycled : confirmed Recycle\ncompletes
Moved --> InReview : undo Move [E]
Managed --> Missing : reconciliation\n[unblocked; file absent]
legend bottom
  Candidate states are analytical and transient. Readiness can become stale.
  Arrows describe completed outcomes, including recovery; failures do not assert a new file state.
  E = eligible undo: latest matching, unchanged, unblocked action; destination free; not already undone.
  Missing has no automatic restoration; completed Recycle has no in-app undo.
endlegend
@enduml
